{"format":"edusim-world","version":1,"exportedAt":"2026-08-16T22:56:37.013Z","label":"Ellis Island","spawn":{"x":0,"z":112,"yaw":0},"records":[{"id":"03a97d77-50ed-4354-8869-ddd8b3edf827","kind":"world-theme","theme":"ellis","createdAt":1786920996929,"transform":{"position":[0,0,0],"rotation":[0,0,0],"scale":[1,1,1]}},{"id":"3e6db382-399b-41fe-8f42-0974f11c0364","createdAt":1786920996931,"transform":{"position":[0,-2.6645352591003757e-15,12],"rotation":[0,0,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"ellis-main-building","options":{"width":76,"depth":36,"height":27,"seed":5}},{"id":"e04dcbc0-93cc-42fa-bfb9-16efca729f96","createdAt":1786920996932,"transform":{"position":[-22,-4.440892098500626e-15,52],"rotation":[0,0.35144479400355166,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"info-placard","options":{"eyebrow":"1892 – 1954","title":"The Main Building","accent":"#a8593c","body":"Twelve million people came through this door. On the busiest single day, 17 April 1907, 11,747 were processed. Red brick with limestone trim and four copper domes — and for most arrivals this was the first American building they ever saw, from the deck of a ship."}},{"id":"e555a2e8-d5e2-4b17-ba6a-748acd8b031b","createdAt":1786920996934,"transform":{"position":[-132,-0.22038314846380214,-68],"rotation":[0,0.9,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"statue-of-liberty","options":{"scale":0.5,"seed":11}},{"id":"8d6dabef-90b9-4b5e-9c02-1454544e8c70","createdAt":1786920996935,"transform":{"position":[-60,-0.04117250069977185,60],"rotation":[0,0.8567056281827385,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"info-placard","options":{"eyebrow":"Look at her feet","title":"The broken chain","accent":"#74b09a","body":"Almost nobody sees it, because you cannot from the ground: she is stepping out of a broken shackle. The statue was a gift from France marking the end of slavery as much as independence. The seven rays of her crown stand for the seven continents and seas."}},{"id":"cbf94dee-f04c-4115-858e-48cdee723724","createdAt":1786920996937,"transform":{"position":[-96,-0.08615573665235932,4],"rotation":[0,0,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"water-body","options":{"width":130,"depth":150,"seed":23,"shore":false}},{"id":"2c6d3477-0001-4f08-879a-3021ca28aeb1","createdAt":1786920996938,"transform":{"position":[104,0.27297501965144066,30],"rotation":[0,0,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"water-body","options":{"width":120,"depth":150,"seed":27,"shore":false}},{"id":"27fd9058-cff2-4f3d-9925-50f72152ea2b","createdAt":1786920996940,"transform":{"position":[-46,-0.050013419760882805,76],"rotation":[0,0.2,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"ferry-pier","options":{"length":46,"width":16,"seed":23}},{"id":"9c527a69-3f45-49ad-ac30-5c8a8299c541","createdAt":1786920996941,"transform":{"position":[-80,-0.15535638681823816,52],"rotation":[0,1.5,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"steamship","options":{"length":100,"funnels":2,"seed":17}},{"id":"23fa3ed3-e8e1-4e15-bce2-5bef61074d0f","createdAt":1786920996943,"transform":{"position":[-40,-0.025037673871174615,62],"rotation":[0,0.6747409422235527,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"info-placard","options":{"eyebrow":"How you got here","title":"Steerage","accent":"#24262b","body":"First and second class passengers were inspected in their cabins and walked straight off at Manhattan. Only steerage came to Ellis Island. Steerage was below the waterline at the stern, over the propellers — a fortnight in the noisiest, roughest berth on the ship, for about $30."}},{"id":"96b2a7fc-c41d-4335-8aa8-f783a62c68e2","createdAt":1786920996944,"transform":{"position":[-20,-0.0017103769481106035,62],"rotation":[0,0.3,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"baggage-pile","options":{"count":30,"spread":10,"seed":29}},{"id":"2562fa25-9b37-4b42-98ed-412b1ac3db70","createdAt":1786920996946,"transform":{"position":[22,0.0001895284627209115,58],"rotation":[0,-0.4,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"baggage-pile","options":{"count":22,"spread":8,"seed":33}},{"id":"cf3986bd-7ea0-4a6b-955a-04eb36f2af56","createdAt":1786920996947,"transform":{"position":[2,-0.00011651705364856824,66],"rotation":[0,-0.04345089539153084,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"info-placard","options":{"eyebrow":"Everything they owned","title":"The baggage","accent":"#6b4a2c","body":"You could bring what you could carry. People arrived with a trunk, or a bundle tied in a sheet, and left it in a heap on this dock while they were examined. Some never got it back. The photographs of the baggage room are the ones that carry the weight of the whole place."}},{"id":"4411cc88-8331-4111-928c-baf4795420ae","createdAt":1786920996949,"transform":{"position":[-6,-8.881784197001252e-15,40],"rotation":[0,0.1,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"inspection-line","options":{"length":28,"seed":31}},{"id":"73a0c742-034c-4e62-8697-12cc28458948","createdAt":1786920996950,"transform":{"position":[24,-9.325873406851315e-15,42],"rotation":[0,-0.3302973548292537,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"info-placard","options":{"eyebrow":"Six seconds a person","title":"The line inspection","accent":"#3a3f45","body":"Doctors watched you walk up the stairs — that was the first test, and you never knew it was happening. At the top they looked at your eyes with a buttonhook for trachoma. A chalk letter on your coat meant a second look: E for eyes, H for heart, X for suspected mental illness. About 2% were sent back."}},{"id":"bf23c98b-44f9-48d1-b6c0-5e0723657b09","createdAt":1786920996952,"transform":{"position":[30,0.021643073926644885,74],"rotation":[0,-0.668289418830584,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"manifest-board","options":{"ship":"SS PRINZESSIN","date":"17 APRIL 1907","souls":"1,806","seed":37}},{"id":"0e50df22-bc25-4cf2-ba6f-c0f6905430d9","createdAt":1786920996953,"transform":{"position":[-30,-0.0287111094