#7fd4c4","depth":1},{"cat":"control","text":"wait 1 seconds","depth":1}],"tip":"The statue was a dull brown when it arrived — it is copper, and copper turns green as it weathers. It took about thirty years. When people proposed painting it back to brown in 1906 the public would not have it.","accent":"#74b09a"}},{"id":"8201b379-3561-4b64-80ca-d7f24b260302","createdAt":1786920997011,"transform":{"position":[0,6.999999999999995,26],"rotation":[0,0,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"light-orb","color":"#f2a541"},{"id":"e3645bee-eaf8-47b4-855d-c588fa4adc5e","createdAt":1786920997012,"transform":{"position":[-6,5.999999999999991,40],"rotation":[0,0,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"light-orb","color":"#f5f5f5"},{"id":"aaebd90f-30ce-4657-a4f0-f44509f47145","createdAt":1786920997013,"transform":{"position":[-132,33.7796168515362,-68],"rotation":[0,0,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"light-orb","color":"#f2a541"}]}